# Base URL of the Task Manager backend API.
#
# - Local dev (`npm run dev`): set this to call the backend directly, e.g.
#     VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8080
#   Vite inlines this at dev-server start / build time (see vite.config.ts).
#
# - Docker / docker-compose: leave VITE_API_URL unset (or empty). The app is
#   served by nginx, which proxies relative `/api/*` requests to the
#   `backend` service (see nginx.conf) — no build-time URL needed.
#
# - Standalone Docker build against a real deployed backend (e.g. Cloud Run):
#   pass it as a build arg so it gets baked into the static bundle, since
#   Vite env vars are not available at container runtime:
#     docker build --build-arg VITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com -t frontend .
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8080
